 "description": "Deterministic country evidence for the country resolver (design docs/country-resolution-design-2026-10-30.md). names: explicit country names, adjectives and sub-national names (E1/E2). authorities: governed tax authorities and central banks (E3). Registry terms (E4) are in country_terms.json. ambiguous_candidates: shared terms that never resolve alone and give a candidate set (null = too broad to narrow). counterparty_role_nouns: a party defined by its role in a transaction (client, supplier...): the other party when a country qualifies it after a preposition or a transaction verb. counterparty_entity_nouns: a party defined only as an entity (company, business, group...): the other party only after a transaction verb, or as the group/parent an entity belongs to. tax_words: words a country name can qualify ('UK VAT', 'German trade tax', 'taxed in Australia'); a country that qualifies the tax is the tax country and outranks the roles. framework_words: a country name followed by one of these is an accounting/auditing framework, not a country. name_exclusions: non-tax uses of a country word. Not live-verified; review before production use. tax_modifiers: the only words allowed between a qualifying country and its tax word ('German trade tax', 'US FICA social security'), so 'a UK group pay corporate tax' does not qualify.",
